{"id":"R0703","study_type":"Human–AI Collaboration Framework; AI-Avatar case study in a simulated cyber range","RQ1 task_stage":"Monitoring, protection, threat detection, alert triage, and incident response","RQ1 domain":"Security Operations Centers (SOCs); IT, operational technology (OT), and cloud settings","RQ1 orientation":"Defensive; SOC described as a proactive defensive hub","RQ2 architecture":"Five autonomy levels mapped to HITL roles and task-specific trust thresholds; ChatGPT-based AI-Avatar with RAG, knowledge graphs, SIEM, IDS, and firewalls","RQ2 llm_used":"ChatGPT-based LLM; version not stated","RQ2 adaptation":"Fine-tuning, RAG, and knowledge graphs; training with wargaming, event data, and Red/Blue Team exercises","RQ3 autonomy_level":"Framework spans manual operations to comprehensive SOC functions with minimal human involvement; AI-Avatar aids analysts in threat detection, triage, and response","RQ3 hitl":"Explicit analyst approval for critical actions at Level 2; exceptional-case intervention at Level 3; periodic audit and strategic oversight at Level 4","RQ4 dataset":"Wargaming, event data, and Red/Blue Team exercises; named datasets not stated","RQ4 environment":"Simulated cyber range; simulated SOC with SIEM, IDS, and firewalls","RQ4 metrics":"not stated","RQ4 baseline_type":"not stated","RQ4 headline_result":"not stated","RQ4 compared_to":"not stated","RQ4 code_available":"not stated","RQ4 data_available":"not stated","RQ5 risks_addressed":"Automation complacency, automation bias, loss of oversight, misclassifications, overtrust and undertrust; adversarial inputs and limited interpretability","RQ5 mitigations":"Dynamic autonomy and HITL calibration by task complexity, risk, and trust; explainable justifications, uncertainty scoring, continuous monitoring, and human oversight","author_limitations (verbatim)":"While NIST CSF 2.0 includes a dedicated \"Governance\" function, governance aspects from a Human–AI collaboration perspective within SOCs are considered out of scope for this article","author_future_work (verbatim)":"not stated","evidence (page/section)":"Abstract and §1 (pp. 1–3): framework, tasks, AI-Avatar, model, adaptation, training data, and simulation; §§3–4.4 (pp. 9–16): architecture, autonomy, HITL, risks, and mitigations; §2.3 footnote 1 (p. 7): scope limitation. Provided text ends during §4.5; evaluation, limitations, and future-direction sections are not included."}
